                {
                  "key": "llm.output_messages.1.message.contents.0.message_content.text",
                  "value": {
                    "stringValue": "An **agent trace** is a record of what an AI agent did during a task, in order. It commonly includes the agent’s inputs and outputs, tool calls and their results, state changes, timestamps, and any errors.\n\nFor example:\n\n1. User asks for the weather.\n2. Agent calls a weather tool for a location.\n3. The tool returns a forecast.\n4. Agent replies with the forecast.\n\nTraces help people **debug, evaluate, and monitor** an agent. They usually record observable steps and tool interactions—not necessarily the agent’s private internal reasoning."
                  }
                },
                {
                  "key": "llm.output_messages.1.message.content",
                  "value": {
                    "stringValue": "An **agent trace** is a record of what an AI agent did during a task, in order. It commonly includes the agent’s inputs and outputs, tool calls and their results, state changes, timestamps, and any errors.\n\nFor example:\n\n1. User asks for the weather.\n2. Agent calls a weather tool for a location.\n3. The tool returns a forecast.\n4. Agent replies with the forecast.\n\nTraces help people **debug, evaluate, and monitor** an agent. They usually record observable steps and tool interactions—not necessarily the agent’s private internal reasoning."
                  }
